    "description": {
      "value": "The Nantambu Chime-Ringers created these magical chimes to aid in their defense of their city. Each chime is made from elaborately carved wood depicting the nature of a given chime's power. You ring the chime, unleashing its magic. The specifics of each chime, as well as the activation's frequency (if any), appear in its entry below. This chime features carvings of destructive runes. When activated, it creates the effects of a 3rd-level sound burst centered on you (DC 20 Fortitude save). Instead of the spell's normal range, it has a 5-foot emanation. In addition, creatures that critically fail their save are knocked prone by the chime's effect. You can use this chime once per day."
    },
